GC: heap corruption under REPL top-level HANDLER-CASE churn

SYMPTOM
-------
Feeding a long sequence (~120) of top-level HANDLER-CASE-wrapped forms to
the bocl REPL on stdin corrupts the process after 15-70 forms.  Observed
manifestations (they DRIFT with binary layout and file content — classic
heap corruption):
  - a C type_error signalled inside a HANDLER-CASE finds NO handler
    (signal_condition walks g_frame_stack and misses the frame), so the
    process prints "In some function: TYPE ERROR: ..." and exit(65);
  - functions misbehave mid-run: (string-greaterp 'abd 'abc) — which
    passed 20 forms earlier — suddenly raises TYPE ERROR SYMBOL/STRING;
  - the run falls into the debug REPL and hangs with a backtrace of
    stacked dynamic-binding frames.

BOCL_NOGC=1 makes the whole sequence pass (121/121) — it is a GC bug:
some Ref reachable only from a C local or a frame parameter is not in
the rootset when a collection triggers, and the collected block's reuse
corrupts the class graph / frame stack / function bindings.

REPRO
-----
tests/test_designators.c exercises the same forms through bocl_test_eval
and passes — the corruption needs the REPL top-level path (%REPL-EVAL +
handler-case frames + the printer echo between forms).  Repro recipe:

  1. Generate a file of ~120 top-level probes of the shape
        (handler-case (let ((r <form>)) (if (equal r <expect>) ...))
          (error (c) ...))
     mixing package ops (intern/export/shadow with designators), string
     functions on symbols, sequence functions with 'symbol function
     designators, and with-output-to-string stream forms.  The probe file
     used for the diagnosis: see the designator audit in
     issues/closed/find-symbol-package.issue (2026-07-15) — any similar
     mixture reproduces within ~70 forms.
  2. ./bocl < probes.lisp        -> dies/hangs between form ~15 and ~72
     BOCL_NOGC=1 ./bocl < probes.lisp -> 121/121 PASS, exit 0.

Simple accumulations do NOT reproduce: 25x (handler-case (+ 1 i) ...)
then a C type error is caught fine.  The trigger needs the mixture
(allocation pressure from format/equal/with-output-to-string between the
handler frames).

TOOLS
-----
BOCL_POISON=1 (+BOCL_POISON_BT=1) exists for exactly this class of bug
(use-after-free finder with per-free backtraces) but is very slow under
the prelude load; run it on a machine with time or trim the prelude.
Suspects to audit first: frame parameters (handler.clauses/condition)
reachability during GC, %REPL-EVAL's live-pool discipline around
signal_condition's longjmp (pools opened by the erring builtin are
never closed), and printer echo allocations between forms.
